n": "", "sign": ""}, {"page": 0, "number": 3861, "suffix": "B", "reference": "", "newEdition": "", "secondaryLiterature": "", "museumNumber": null, "cdliNumber": "", "externalProject": "", "notes": "", "date": "", "transliteration": "", "sign": ""}, {"page": 0, "number": 3862, "suffix": "B", "reference": "", "newEdition": "", "secondaryLiterature": "", "museumNumber": null, "cdliNumber": "", "externalProject": "", "notes": "", "date": "", "transliteration": "", "sign": ""}, {"page": 0, "number": 3863, "suffix": "B", "reference": "", "newEdition": "", "secondaryLiterature": "", "museumNumber": null, "cdliNumber": "", "externalProject": "", "notes": "", "date": "", "transliteration": "", "sign": ""}, {"page": 0, "number": 3864, "suffix": "B", "reference": "", "newEdition": "", "secondaryLiterature": "", "museumNumber": null, "cdliNumber": "", "externalProject": "", "notes": "", "date": "", "transliteration": "", "sign": ""}, {"page": 0, "number": 3865, "suffix": "B", "reference": "", "newEdition": "", "secondaryLiterature": "", "museumNumber": null, "cdliNumber": "", "externalProject": "", "notes": "", "date": "", "transliteration": "", "sign": ""}, {"page": 0, "number": 3866, "suffix": "B", "reference": "", "newEdition": "", "secondaryLiterature": "", "museumNumber": null, "cdliNumber": "", "externalProject": "", "notes": "", "date": "", "transliteration": "", "sign": ""}, {"page": 0, "number": 3867, "suffix": "B", "reference": "", "newEdition": "", "secondaryLiterature": "", "museumNumber": null, "cdliNumber": "", "externalProject": "", "notes": "", "date": "", "transliteration": "", "sign": ""}], "mesZl": "92\t**PAB**\t𒉽\t→ Kap. VII\nASy 32. Lww. pap (n.); bab/p (n); pa₄ (altakk. in pa₄-šiš? siehe unten auf dieser Seite; bab. a. in pappāsu, AHw 824b oben, CAD P 111f.); ba₁₄ (altakk., CAD B 178a) — kúr (n.).\n---\npap, pa₄ = *aḫu*, Bruder (N.P.). ^I^PAB-*bu-u* usw. = *àḫa-bu-u* (Deller, OrNS 34 262).\nkúr = *nakāru*, anders, feindlich s./w. Cf Thureau-D., TMB p233.\n(^lú^)kúr = *nakru*, Feind. en ^lú^kúr sowie en ^lú^kúr-meš = Erzfeind? (akkadische Lesung unsicher, siehe Borger, BIWA 109 zu B VII 8; CAD N/I 171b s.v. bēl nakāri). CAD N/II 332 bietet für en kúr auch die Lesung *bēl nukurti*.\nMUNUS-kúr siehe n883.\npap = *napḫar*(*u*), Summe. Nach Parpola, OLZ 74 28 neuassyr. statt *napḫar*(*u*) wohl *gimir* oder *gamir* zu lesen.\nPAB = *naṣāru*, bewachen (besonders in N.P.).\nPAB = *pappu* o.ä., das Zeichen PAB (CAD P 114b; anders AHw 824b).\nkúr als Korrekturzeichen. Cf Lambert, Fs. Kraus 216; Maul, Zukunftsbewältigung 440 Anm. 13, Wiggermann, Mesopotamian protective spirits p129f.; Cooper, Gs. Sachs 90; Civil, MSL 14 6f. Boissier, Choix I 137; Bezold, Cat. zu K 2111, K 6744, 81-2-4,228, 83-1-18,421+ (CT 31 9ff.); MSL 1 54 50^!^ = Borger, NAWG 1991/II [18] unten; CT 39 38; CT 41 27 left edge (CAD A/I 246b Mitte); Bīt mēsiri nach meiner Rekonstruktion z. 2+c (SpTU II n8 III 13’, siehe die Kopie).\n𒉽𒄬 siehe n93.\n𒉽𒉽 siehe n94.\n^dingir^𒉽𒈛 = *pap-sukkal*.\n𒉽𒂊 siehe n96.\n𒉽𒋀 = pa₄-šiš, *pa*₄-*šiš* (Seux, Epithètes 222, CAD P 253ff.)? Eher mit Krispijn, Fs. Pettinato 105f.: pa₄-šeš = “Ältester”, cf CAD A/I 195b und 204f.\n𒉽𒊺𒉽 usw. siehe n94.\n^dingir^𒉽𒌋𒌓𒆤𒃻𒊏 = *pa*₄-*nìgin*/*nig*₆/*ni*₉-*gar-ra* (Krecher, SKLy 128ff.).\n𒉆𒉽 = nam-kúr = *nakrūtu* oder *nukurtu*? Feindschaft.", "LaBaSi": "67", "reverseOrder": "", "unicode": [74365], "sortKeys": {"neoAssyrianOnset": [90], "neoBabylonianOnset": [18, 31, 571], "neoAssyrianOffset": [11], "neoBabylonianOffset": [41]}, "name": "PAP"}